0 Type///Basidiocarp very small to large. pluteoid; lamellae free, pink-coloured with age; volva and annulus absent; spore print pinkish brown.rust-brown.///Spores mainly subglobose to ellipsoid, uniguttulate, with moderately thick (up to 1 um) wall, smooth, non-amyloid, cyanophylous;///basidia 4-spored. rarely 1- or 2-spored; cheilocystidia present; p1euroeystidia in most species present; hymenophoral trama inverse; pileipellis a cutis, a trichoderm or a hymeniderm; stipitipellis a cutis without or with caulocystidia; clamp-connections absent. more rarely present; pigment intracellular, in some species also extracellular; refractive hyphae present. ///- Type species: Agaricus pluteus Batsch: Fr. (= Pluteus cervinus(Schaeff.) Kumm.).///HABITAT & DISTRIBUTION - Saprophytic, on wood or terrestrial. Cosmopolitan.011113700
